{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Choice spices.</b> Precious ones." "<b>And cinnamon, fragrant.</b> Since cinnamon is the bark of a tree — there are some that are good and have good fragrance and taste, and there are some that are merely like wood — therefore it needed to say קִנְּמָן בֹּשֶׂם — of the good kind." "<b>Half of it two hundred and fifty.</b> Half of its hin shall be two hundred and fifty, so that all of it is five hundred, the same measure as pure myrrh. If so, why is it stated in halves? It is a decree of Scripture to bring it to halves, to increase in it two weightings — for one does not weigh eye for eye; and so it is taught in Karetot." "<b>And cane, fragrant.</b> A cane of fragrance; since there are canes that are not of fragrance, it needed to say קְנֵה בֹשֶׂם." "<b>Two hundred and fifty.</b> The total weight of all of it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:48.872568689Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}